ng different identity facts in hello and certificate; contracts.rpc other than [\"5.0.0\"]; Structured Error version drift), timeout/race (silent peer past the handshake and hello deadlines; a peer stalling mid-request against the configured RPC timeout; two concurrent connections from one peer), custody (leaf private key read from a wrong-permission file or a foreign store refused by the ResolvedPaths pair; a copied key authenticates until revoked — assert both halves as the pinned text states), revocation and generation (revoke a live peer: idle and in-flight streams close within one second per the pinned text — measure it; rotation admits the new tuple only after explicit enrollment, retire_at bounds, no second rotation before revocation; a stale generation at dispatch and at a mutation boundary refused under concurrent mutation), migration/downgrade refusals (Config-4 selecting a legacy route, an RPC-4 hello on the host channel, a plaintext preface), both role failures (initiator refuses a bad server; responder refuses a bad client), stale/failed reads (an unreadable trust store or marker is an integrity failure, not \"absent\"), recovery bypasses (a retry that changes the operation ID or body is refused; no new-session/fresh-handle substitution); (3) every vector asserts the exact Section 15 class and exit and that nothing durable changed (census the state dir before/after); (4) the Section 11.10.5 upstream policy vectors are source evidence only — do not implement a policy reader and do not claim their synthetic passes as executed support; (5) narrowing mutants for every new assertion family with a shipped harness (per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control), plus the seven original conformance cases of this task re-derived with n-of-m through the authenticated channel; (6) a conformance matrix mapping every AC-HOST-001 clause, HC-* gate and hostile-network row to a test, a not-executed stated bound (native Tailscale SSH; platfo